<title>BRAZIL: Brazil grains/oilseeds crop to rise in 1997 - Safras.</title>
<headline>Brazil grains/oilseeds crop to rise in 1997 - Safras.</headline>
<dateline>RIO DE JANEIRO 1996-11-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's grains and oilseed crop should reach 76.45 million tonnes in 1997, up six percent from this year's 72.14 million tonnes, independent consultants Safras e Mercado said in its first estimate.</p>
<p>&quot;This result is basically due to expectations the weather may be more regular than in the current season and that there may be slightly better inevestment in technology,&quot; Safras said.</p>
<p>Planted area is not expected to increase greatly given the continuing credit problems.</p>
<p>&quot;Despite some adjustments in trading policy in 1996, agriculture in Brazil still lacks definite paths and needs to be treated as a priority,&quot; Safras said.</p>
<p>The 1997 estimate is still below the record 77.01 million tonnes obtained in 1995, it added.</p>
<p>Principal crops included in the Safras e Mercado forecast were as follows in 1,000 tonnes.</p>
<p> CROP		    1997		1996	    PCT CHANGE</p>
<p> Rice		   9,550	    10,153	     -6</p>
<p> Oats		     190		 188		1</p>
<p> Barley		   166		 166		0</p>
<p> Black beans	  3,000	     2,886		4</p>
<p> Corn		  33,470	    30,462	     10</p>
<p> Sorghum		  330		 327		1</p>
<p> Wheat		  1,870	     3,035	    -38</p>
<p> Palm/palm kernel     421		 421		0</p>
<p> Soybeans	    26,378	    23,294	     13</p>
<p>-- Caroline Bulloch, Rio de Janeiro newsroom, 5521 5074151</p>
